    {
      "id": "e9000065-0000-4000-8000-000000000065",
      "name": "Sticky Keys",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Keys\n`Load workflow config` is the only place with tunable values (the workflow's env). Edit `businessRules` to change the bot's behaviour. Secrets are n8n credentials, never here: `WAHA account` (URL + API key), `OpenAI account`, `Postgres account`.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e9000066-0000-4000-8000-000000000066",
      "name": "Sticky 1 Receive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · Receive\nWAHA posts `message.any` to the trigger (only that output is wired). Two Set nodes map the raw payload to one normalized message (Extract pulls the raw fields, Normalize derives type and chat kind): `messageId, session, chatId, senderId, fromMe, type, text, timestamp, isGroup, isDirect`. Protocol events get `type: protocol` and are dropped by the first guard.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e9000067-0000-4000-8000-000000000067",
      "name": "Sticky 2 Guards",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        690,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · Guards\nEach Filter drops the item silently: own messages, groups/broadcasts/channels and chats outside the allow-list; then duplicates (`messageId` already stored); then chats answered less than `perChatMinIntervalSeconds` ago.",
        "height": 560,
        "width": 1200,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e9000068-0000-4000-8000-000000000068",
      "name": "Sticky 3 Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1940,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · Reply\nText gets an LLM reply (memory keyed by `chatId`); other types get `unsupportedTypeReply`. An LLM error or empty reply sends `failureReply`. All three set the same `{ text, replyKind }`.",
        "height": 840,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e9000069-0000-4000-8000-000000000069",
      "name": "Sticky 4 Send",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2940,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 · Send like a human\nSeen → wait → typing for a length-based delay → stop typing → send. Presence calls are best-effort; the send is never retried.",
        "height": 840,
        "width": 1700,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e9000070-0000-4000-8000-000000000070",
      "name": "Sticky 5 Outcome",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4680,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 · Outcome\nStamps the last reply time. A failed send or an LLM failure fails the execution once, so the error workflow runs once.",
        "height": 840,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 7
      }
    }
